# taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations

[![Documentation](https://docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/projects/taf-ul-oam_kpi_calculations/badge/)][1]
[![Requirements](https://taf.wrgitlab-pages.int.net.nokia.com/miscellaneous/static-badges/requirements.svg)](requirements/base.txt)
[![build status](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations/badges/main/pipeline.svg)][2]
[![coverage report](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations/badges/main/coverage.svg)][2]
[![latest release](https://wrgitlab.int.net.nokia.com/TAF/taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations/-/badges/release.svg)][3]

## Supported Python versions

Library should work properly with Python versions specified within
`python_requires` option in [setup.py](setup.py).

## Installation

Generic library installation process is described in [TAF user guide][4].

# Overview
Library allows calculate OAM KPI based on IMS snapshot. You can use library directly in Robot Framework test case or as standalone library.

>__Note__
>
>For KPI related to Site Reset, SW Upgrade etc it's important to use IMS snapshot from admin session([collect_infomodel_log_from_current_session](https://taf-sbts-oam-coam-admin.docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/en/latest/interfaces/interface.html#taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin.interface.admin.collect_infomodel_log_from_current_session) keyword). Only this snapshot contains entry about RST 
>
>![RST Entry](images/rst.jpg)
> 
>For other KPIs you can use snapshot collected by KW [collect_im_snapshot](https://taf-sbts-oam-coam-admin.docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/en/latest/interfaces/interface.html#taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin.interface.admin.collect_im_snapshot)  too
> 
>For better accuracy please set `update_interval` parameter to 500 ms in [`connect_to`](https://taf-sbts-oam-coam-admin.docs.taf.ute.nsn-rdnet.net/en/latest/interfaces/interface.html#taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin.interface.admin.connect_to) method

