## Calculate KPI Using Specific cell_dist_names
If you are interested in particular cells, you can pass the `cell_dist_names` parameter. Only the specified `cell_dist_names` will be used for KPI calculation. In other cases, all cells from IMS will be used.
This parameter should not be overused; it should be utilized only when absolutely necessary.
```python
from taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations import oam_kpi_calculations
oam_kpi = oam_kpi_calculations()
oam_kpi.calculate_kpi1a(ims_file_path='/home/ute/IMS/KPI_site_reset.ims2',
                        cell_dist_names=[
                            '/MRBTS-1/RAT-1/RUNTIME_VIEW-1/MRBTS_R-1/LNBTS_R-47212/LNCEL_R-1'
                            '/MRBTS-1/RAT-1/RUNTIME_VIEW-1/MRBTS_R-1/LNBTS_R-47212/LNCEL_R-2'
                        ])
oam_kpi.save_results_to_file(file_path='/home/ute/IMS/kpi1a.json')
```

## Calculate own KPI
To calculate your own KPI based on cell events, you can use the `calculate_kpi_using_cell_up_down_events` method.
The interface is similar to other KPI calculation methods. Additionally, you need to specify the `cell_down_start_point` and `cell_up_end_point` parameters, which can be either `first` or `last` events. You also need to provide your own `kpi_name`.

```python 
from taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations import oam_kpi_calculations
oam_kpi = oam_kpi_calculations()
oam_kpi.calculate_kpi_using_cell_up_down_events(kpi_name='my_own_kpi',
                                                cell_down_start_point='first',
                                                cell_up_end_point='last')
oam_kpi.save_results_to_file(file_path='/home/ute/IMS/my_own_kpi.json')
```

This method allows for flexible KPI calculations based on specific cell events, enabling you to tailor the KPI to your specific needs.
Please avoid overusing this method. It is preferable to use predefined KPIs. If a KPI has not been defined yet, please contact me.

## Special KPIs which requires pass start_point_timestamp(eg: KPI3)
```python
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from taf.ul.oam_kpi_calculations import oam_kpi_calculations
oam_kpi = oam_kpi_calculations()
# Power ON BTS
bts_power_on_timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc)
# wait till BTS up
# collect IMS snapshot
oam_kpi.calculate_kpi3(ims_file_path='/home/ute/IMS/KPI_power_reset.ims2', start_point_timestamp=bts_power_on_timestamp)
results = oam_kpi.get_results() # You can use it it for further actions like: report/verification 
```

## KPI2
To calculate KPI2 you need IMS from admin session. During Software Upgrade, connection to admin is disconnected and IMS file is automatic saved in `${OUTPUT_DIR}` location.
<br>Thus to calculate KPIs you need to use 2 IMS files: one before upgrade and second after.
>__Note__
> Please notice that you need to pass IMS files in chronological order.

<br>To check ims file path from disconnected session you can use KW `get_last_disconnected_ims_log`
<br>For more details please check `Sample Software Upgrade` from [Sample_robot.md](examples/Sample_Robot.md)


## Example in Robot
```robot
*** Settings ***
Library  interface.oam_kpi  WITH NAME  oam_kpi

*** Test Cases ***
Sample Test Case
    # Test Setup
    
    oam_kpi.save_search_start_timestamp  # optional
    
    # Main operation like block/unblock
    
    oam_kpi.save_search_end_timestamp   # optional
    
    # Collect IMS snapshot(taf.sbts.oam.coam.admin library):
    ## for site reset you need to use KW: collect_infomodel_log_from_current_session
    ## for any other operation you could use KW: collect_im_snapshot
    
    oam_kpi.calculate_kpi17a  ims_file_path=//home/ute/temp/ims/block_unblock.ims2  global_cell_id=54
    
    # Do other staff
    ${results}  oam_kpi.get_results
    # You can use results for further actions like: report/verification 

    oam_kpi.save_results_to_file  file_path=/home/ute/auto/robotws/testsuite/Krakow/resources/oam_kpi/file.json
```

# FAQ
## KPIs weren't calculated and results is empty
If you have results like eg: 
```json
{
    "kpi1a": [],
    "kpi1b": [],
    "kpi1c": []
}
```
Generally if output is empty it means that `indication_point`/`start_point` was not detected.
<br>As first please check:
* if you are using proper IMS file - if Site reset you need to use IMS from admin session.
* if RST request is visible in admin timeline(if site reset KPI)

If in your opinion everything is OK, most probably something wrong is in library and needs some adaptations(usually regex improvement). So please contact to author.


